  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "For the peanut sauce, peel one garlic clove and chop it finely or press it. Stir it together with the peanut butter, soy sauce, 5 g of honey and a little lemon zest and lemon juice. Gradually add water until the sauce is creamy. Taste and set aside."
    },
    {
      "text": "Peel the carrots and cut them into thin sticks or slices. Peel the onion and cut it into wedges. Peel the second garlic clove and chop it finely."
    },
    {
      "text": "Toss the vegetables with the garlic, 5 g of honey, the oil, sesame seeds and teriyaki sauce. Cook in the air fryer at 150 °C for about 14 minutes. Turn them halfway through and cook a little longer if needed until the carrots are as tender as you like.",
      "timerMinutes": 14
    },
    {
      "text": "Cut the chicken breast into two cutlets of even thickness and pound them a little flatter if needed."
    },
    {
      "text": "Put the flour, beaten egg and panko on three separate plates. Coat the chicken first in flour, then in egg and finally in panko. Press the coating on lightly."
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat the oil in a deep pan or pot. Fry the chicken cutlets over medium-high heat until golden brown on both sides and cooked through. Drain on kitchen paper."
    },
    {
      "text": "Meanwhile, prepare the udon noodles in hot water according to the package instructions and drain them."
    },
    {
      "text": "Gently warm the peanut sauce in a pot. Toss it with the udon noodles and add a little water if needed."
    },
    {
      "text": "Slice the chicken katsu into strips. Divide the noodles and vegetables between two plates and arrange the chicken on top."
    }
  ]
